# Scoped overrides for the wrapper forwarding layer. Merged onto the repo-root
# .clang-tidy (InheritParentConfig), so every other check there still applies
# here -- this file only turns off the two that are structurally wrong for this
# subtree.
#
# src/wrappers/ is a thin, dispatch-checked forwarding surface: each function
# mirrors a vendor BLAS/SOLVER/FFT/SPARSE entry point by NAME and by SIGNATURE
# (see the token-paste forwards these expand to). So the whole public API is
# intentionally vendor-cased (gemm, getrfBatched, csr2gebsr_bufferSize) and
# takes the vendor's C-array parameters (T *const A[]); neither follows the
# house style, and neither can without breaking the forward. Suppressing at each
# site would mean hundreds of NOLINTs restating one fact about the directory.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-identifier-naming,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays
